# The mirror workflow checks the PRIVATE monorepo out here, then runs
# `git add -A` in this PUBLIC repository. Because that checkout carries its
# own .git, git currently stages it as a gitlink rather than as files, so the
# private source is not published today - but the private HEAD sha is, and a
# bogus submodule entry lands on main. That safety depends entirely on
# .monorepo/.git existing. Ignoring the path removes the dependency instead
# of relying on it.
#
# No trailing slash: a directory-only pattern ("<name>/") is not reported as
# ignored when the path does not exist yet, which would leave the rule
# unverifiable in a clean checkout.
.monorepo
